   "text": {
    "L1": "Division makes equal groups or groups of a given size.",
    "L2": "We divide from the left: hundreds, then tens, then ones.",
    "L3": "Watch 735 divided by 7. Seven hundreds divided by seven gives one hundred.",
    "L4": "Three tens is too small to divide by seven, so write zero in the tens place.",
    "L5": "Bring down to make 35 ones. Thirty-five divided by seven gives five.",
    "L6": "The quotient is 105. The zero is important because it keeps the place value correct.",
    "L7": "Check by multiplying the quotient by the divisor. Then add any remainder.",
    "L8": "Now choose the quotient for 618 divided by 6."
   },
